## UI patterns — site-wide

### Table (kt-datatable)
Every table on the site uses `kt-datatable`. Row element IDs follow: `#${tableId}_row_${recordId}`

```typescript
// Get a row by record ID
const row = myWhamPage.table.getRowById('myWhamSearchTable', 2525);

// Read a cell by its data-field name
const level = await myWhamPage.table.getCellText(row, 'Level');

// Wait for rows after search
await myWhamPage.table.waitForTableRows(tableLocator);
```

Cells have `data-field` attributes matching column names: `To`, `Category`, `Level`, `Type`, `Properties`, `Message`, `Creation Date`, `Expiration Date`, `Confidential`.

### Checkboxes
Two types in tables:
- **Select all** (header): `selectAllRows(tableLocator)` — aria-label `"select or unselect all rows"`
- **Row checkbox**: `selectRowCheckbox(rowLocator)` — scoped to `[data-field="checkbox"] input`

### Dropdowns
All dropdowns are native `<select>`. Option values are **numeric IDs** — always select by label:
```typescript
// Correct
await page.selectDropdownByLabel(levelDropdown, 'HIGH');

// Wrong — numeric ID may change
await page.selectDropdown(levelDropdown, '3');
```

### Date picker (Bootstrap)
Inputs accept direct typed entry in `MM/DD/YYYY` format:
```typescript
await page.fillDate(expirationInput, '06/30/2026');
// fillDate fills the value and presses Tab to close the picker
```

Only use `selectDateFromPicker` if the field is read-only.

### Spinner
A `.blockui` overlay appears during any loading operation. Always call after clicks that trigger data loads:
```typescript
await page.waitForSpinnerToDisappear();
```

### Saved Criteria bar (reports)
Appears on report pages: `<select>` dropdown + Save / Reset / Delete / Print buttons.
```typescript
await page.selectSavedCriteria('My Search');
await page.clickPrint();
await page.submitReportToQueue('Monthly Assessment Run');
```

### My Process / Report queue
Reports are queued and polled manually. Status badge values: `Start`, `Started`, `Success`, `Error`.
```typescript
await page.searchMyProcess();
const row = page.getRowById('myProcessTable', reportId);
const finalStatus = await page.waitForReportComplete(
    () => page.searchMyProcess(),
    row,
    300_000   // 5 min timeout
);
const links = await page.getResultFileLinks(resultsModal);
```

### New tab
When a report or link opens in a new tab:
```typescript
const reportPage = await page.waitForNewTab(async () => {
    await page.clickElement(exportButton);
});
```

